[Music]  [Music]  [Music]  hello thanks for watching so basically  those exercises I came up with today  because when I first started practicing  I could not play the Beethoven the  opening of the Beethoven sonata with the  double thirds and also the chopin etude  so I decided I would find ways to just  work on double thirds and no parallel  intervals in general and it just grew  from there  so if you're working on that I wish you  good luck because I know how hard it is  and how frustrating it is because a lot  of times it's almost like a tongue  twister cuz you feel like you can get it  it's pretty simple but once you try to  go a little faster or go for a little  longer then it just keeps getting worse  and worse and I think the key though is  to just work on not finger independence  cuz they they really depend on each  other when you're playing parallel  anything but using more of your fingers  rather than your wrists because I have  that problem especially with that etude  I used to use more of my wrist this  rotate rotation motion to get the thirds  from one third to the next but that only  creates problems because you're not  using the tips of your fingers which  will enable you to be more precise and  have more control so that's it thank you  so much again and I'll see you in the  next video bye  [Music]

